  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "For an endothermic reaction, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;H</mi></math> represent the enthalpy of reaction in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>, the minimum value for energy of activation (for forward reaction) will be",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "wQwD2",
      "text": "less than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;H</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "X2hc0",
      "text": "zero",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "VFlSw",
      "text": "more than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;H</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "wa99t",
      "text": "equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;H</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>We know that, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;H</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></msub></math></p><p>where, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo></math> activation energy for backward and forward respectively.</p><p>Thus,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>&#916;H</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></msub></math>, means <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>&#916;H</mi></math>.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><img height=\"147\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/2c2a2389-0aa1-407e-89e8-b543d5c2cc71-image.png\" width=\"240\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;H</mi><mo>=</mo></math>heat of reaction (endothermic)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub><mo>=</mo></math>energy of activation</p><p>Thus, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>&#916;H</mi></math></p><p>Heat is absorbed in an endothermic reaction. Thus, for an endothermic reaction, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;H</mi></math> represent the enthalpy of reaction in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>, the minimum value for energy of activation (for forward reaction) will be&nbsp;more than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;H</mi></math>.</p></blockquote>",
    "image": null
  },
